{"duration_api_ms":47762,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6945e83d-8fac-44a5-906d-349113a7eed0","total_cost_usd":0.1008316,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11095,"cache_read_input_tokens":4538,"output_tokens":5554,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2780},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11095,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5554,"cache_read_input_tokens":4538,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11095,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11095},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":5554,"cacheReadInputTokens":4538,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11095,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1008316,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":2780,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"merged_document\": \"# BIP: 39\\n\\n## Abstract\\nThis BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\\n\\nIt consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed. This seed can be later used to generate deterministic wallets using BIP-0032 or similar methods.\\n\\n## Copyright\\nThis BIP is licensed under the 2-clause BSD license.\\n\\n## Motivation\\nA mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed. The sentence could be written on paper or spoken over the telephone.\\n\\nThis guide is meant to be a way to transport computer-generated determinism with a human-readable transcription. It's not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\\n\\n## Generating the Mnemonic\\nThe mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits. With more entropy security is improved but the sentence length increases. We refer to the initial entropy length as ENT. The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\\n\\nFirst, an initial entropy of ENT bits is generated. A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash. This checksum is appended to the start of the initial entropy. Next, these concatenated bits are split into groups of 12 bits, each encoding a number from 0-2047, serving as an index into a wordlist. Finally, we convert these numbers into words and use the joined words as a mnemonic sentence.\\n\\nThe following table describes the relation between the initial entropy length (ENT), the checksum length (CS), and the length of the generated mnemonic sentence (MS) in words.\\n\\n```\\nCS = ENT / 32\\nMS = (ENT + CS) / 11\\n\\n|  ENT  | CS | ENT+CS |  MS  |\\n+-------+----+--------+------+\\n|  128  |  4 |   132  |  12  |\\n|  160  |  5 |   165  |  15  |\\n|  192  |  6 |   198  |  18  |\\n|  224  |  7 |   231  |  21  |\\n|  256  |  8 |   264  |  24  |\\n```\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0039.mediawiki\",\n  \"decisions\": [\n    {\n      \"slot\": \"heading for the mnemonic-generation section\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        { \"text\": \"## Generating the memonic\", \"document\": \"source_b.md\" }\n      ],\n      \"chosen\": \"## Generating the Mnemonic\",\n      \"reason\": \"only candidate, misspelling and casing corrected\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"dispositions\": [\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a3\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"This BIP describes the implementation of a mnemonic code or mnemonic sentence -- a group of easy to remember words -- for the generation of deterministic wallets.\",\n      \"reason\": \"corrected 'letters' and 'UTOXs' to match the described fact\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a4\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"It consists of two parts: generating the mnemonic and converting it into a binary seed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"'ASCII seed' corrected to the actual binary seed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a7\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"This BIP is licensed under the 2-clause BSD license.\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP-0039's actual copyright license corrected\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a9\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A mnemonic code or sentence is superior for human interaction compared to the handling of raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"'wallet satoshis' corrected to 'wallet seed'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a12\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"It's not a way to process user-created sentences (also known as brainwallets) into a wallet seed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"'süeed' is a misspelling of 'seed'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b1\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"## Generating the Mnemonic\",\n      \"reason\": \"'memonic' misspelling and heading case corrected\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b2\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\n      \"reason\": \"'demonic'/'23 bits' corrected to mnemonic/32 bits\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b5\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\n      \"reason\": \"'1024-2048 byts' corrected to 128-256 bits\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b7\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\n      \"reason\": \"'SHA652' corrected to SHA256\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"mismatch\": \"\",\n  \"additions\": [\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"for the generation of deterministic wallets\",\n      \"corrects\": \"for the generation of deterministic UTOXs\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP39 mnemonics generate deterministic wallets, not UTXOs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"a group of easy to remember words\",\n      \"corrects\": \"a group of easy to remember letters\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"a mnemonic sentence is composed of words, not letters\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"converting it into a binary seed\",\n      \"corrects\": \"converting it into a ASCII seed\",\n      \"basis\": \"citation\",\n      \"source\": \"BIP-0039 specification, Abstract section\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP39 specifies a binary seed, not an ASCII seed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"This BIP is licensed under the 2-clause BSD license.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"This BIP falls under the GPL License.\",\n      \"basis\": \"citation\",\n      \"source\": \"BIP-0039 specification, Copyright section\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP39's actual copyright section names the 2-clause BSD license\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet seed\",\n      \"corrects\": \"raw binary or hexadecimal representations of a wallet satoshis\",\n      \"basis\": \"own-knowledge\",\n      \"source\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"'satoshis' does not fit; the subject being represented is a seed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"The mnemonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 32 bits.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"The demonic must encode entropy in a multiple of 23 bits.\",\n      \"basis\": \"citation\",\n      \"source\": \"BIP-0039 specification, Generating the mnemonic section\",\n      \"reason\": \"entropy must be a multiple of 32 bits per BIP39 and its own table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 128-256 bits.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"The allowed size of ENT is 1024-2048 byts.\",\n      \"basis\": \"citation\",\n      \"source\": \"BIP-0039 specification, Generating the mnemonic section\",\n      \"reason\": \"matches BIP39's own ENT table (128-256)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA256 hash.\",\n      \"corrects\": \"A checksum is generated by taking the first ENT / 32 bits of its SHA652 hash.\",\n      \"basis\": \"citation\",\n      \"source\": \"BIP-0039 specification, Generating the mnemonic section\",\n      \"reason\": \"BIP39 uses SHA256; SHA652 does not exist\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":29777,"type":"result","duration_ms":47830,"uuid":"870ab2c0-4d4f-4053-86b6-db1938448de0","ttft_stream_ms":1927,"time_to_request_ms":69,"first_content_frame_ms":1928,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
